(7786005, 1291606, 36065, '<td valign="top">
<b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b>
<br/>
<br/><b>My thoughts on the image:</b> We may have to rename this the Janine Critique Club, lol.  I don''t think I have ever noticed a tie on a challenge before.  As per normal, lovely capture!  I like the depth of this one, and the way it draws me well into the picture.  I like the centered composition, and the PP is strong on for it.
<br/>
<br/><b>My ideas for improvement: </b> Personally, I probably would have brought up the exposure just a touch, but there isn''t much more that I would have done differently.
<br/>
<br/><b>Where I would have/did score this entry:</b> I did not vote in this challenge, but this one would have been a 6 or 7 for me.  There were several strong entries. Even still, I feel like this one should have finished a few spots stronger.  There were a couple of strong finishers in this one that are head scratchers to me.  Either way, nice image and thanks for sharing!
<br/>
<br/>Thank you for the opportunity to provide a critique on your entry,
<br/><b>Eric</b>
<br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club

My thoughts on the image: We may have to rename this the Janine Critique Club, lol.  I don''t think I have ever noticed a tie on a challenge before.  As per normal, lovely capture!  I like the depth of this one, and the way it draws me well into the picture.  I like the centered composition, and the PP is strong on for it.

My ideas for improvement:  Personally, I probably would have brought up the exposure just a touch, but there isn''t much more that I would have done differently.

Where I would have/did score this entry: I did not vote in this challenge, but this one would have been a 6 or 7 for me.  There were several strong entries. Even still, I feel like this one should have finished a few spots stronger.  There were a couple of strong finishers in this one that are head scratchers to me.  Either way, nice image and thanks for sharing!

Thank you for the opportunity to provide a critique on your entry,
Eric', '2025-08-04 11:01:01.000000', NULL, 0);
